{"type":"message","id":"5545a5a2","parentId":"fd26dc48","timestamp":"2026-06-24T08:38:13.811Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are the coder agent.\n\nTASK ID: task-003\n\nTASK: Foundation: types, config, state, and helper modules\n\nDESCRIPTION:\nCreate the foundation layer for multi-model routing (issue #86). Work on branch `feature/86-multi-model-routing`.\n\n## Steps\n\n### 0. Create feature branch\n```bash\ngit checkout -b feature/86-multi-model-routing\n```\n\n### 1. Read the analysis and existing code\nRead `/home/vedat/work/personal/semblr/temp/issue-86-analysis.md` for full context.\nRead existing code: `lib/semblr-config.ts`, `lib/state.ts`, `src/semblr.ts` to understand conventions.\n\n### 2. Add types\nIn a new section in `lib/semblr-config.ts` (or a new file if that's cleaner), define:\n```typescript\n// Phase names the LLM can self-report\ntype PhaseName = \"thinking\" | \"executing\" | \"stuck\" | \"reporting\" | \"reviewing\" | \"verifying\";\n\n// Map from phase to model ID (null = stay on current model)\ntype PhaseModelMap = Record<PhaseName, string | null>;\n\n// Config for multi-model routing\ninterface MultiModelRoutingConfig {\n  enabled: boolean;        // opt-in, default false\n  maxSwitches: number;     // switch limit per cycle\n  phaseModelMap: PhaseModelMap;\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Add config toggle to `lib/semblr-config.ts`\nAdd `multiModelRouting` to the SemblrConfig interface:\n- `enabled`: boolean, default `false` (opt-in)\n- `maxSwitches`: number, default `3`\n- `phaseModelMap`: PhaseModelMap with the Ollama-Cloud hardcoded map\n\n### 4. Add state fields to `lib/state.ts`\nAdd to the conversation state:\n- `switchCounter: number` (tracks switches per cycle, resets each cycle)\n- `currentPhase: PhaseName | null` (current reported phase)\n- `pendingModelSwitch: string | null` (model to switch to at agent_end)\n\n### 5. Create `lib/resolve-model-id.ts` (NEW FILE)\n```typescript\n// Resolves Ollama-Cloud model IDs like \"glm-5.2:cloud\" to actual provider model IDs\n// For MVP: strip \":cloud\" suffix, keep the base name for ollama provider\nexport function resolveModelId(modelId: string): { provider: string; model: string };\n```\n- If modelId contains \":cloud\", strip it and use \"ollama\" provider\n- Otherwise, pass through as-is\n- Write unit tests alongside\n\n### 6. Create `lib/phase-model-map.ts` (NEW FILE)\nExport the hardcoded MVP phase→model map (from comment #2 on the issue):\n```typescript\nexport const MVP_PHASE_MODEL_MAP: PhaseModelMap = {\n  thinking: null,           // stay on default model for thinking\n  executing: \"glm-5.2:cloud\",\n  stuck: \"kimi-k2.6:cloud\",\n  reporting: \"gemma4:12b:cloud\",\n  reviewing: \"deepseek-v4-pro:cloud\",  \n  verifying: \"deepseek-v4-flash:cloud\",\n};\n```\nAlso export a function `getModelForPhase(phase: PhaseName, map: PhaseModelMap): string | null`.\n\n### 7. Write unit tests\nFor `resolveModelId` and `getModelForPhase`. Follow existing test patterns.\n\n### 8. Verify\n```bash\nnpx tsc --noEmit   # typecheck\nnpx vitest run     # run tests\n```\n\nWrite all findings/decisions to `/home/vedat/work/personal/semblr/temp/task-003-output.md`.\nDo NOT rely on stdout — write all results to files.\n\nComplete this task using available tools. Report STATUS when finished."}],"timestamp":1782290293793}}
